<%#
  Shared vote widget — rendered by the feed card, the show page, AND re-rendered by
  votes/create.turbo_stream.erb. The wrapper id MUST match the Turbo-Stream replace
  target: dom_id(hujah, :vote_bars) => "vote_bars_hujah_<id>".

  Locals: hujah, current_user_vote (one of "agree"/"neutral"/"disagree"/nil).

  VOTE-FEEDBACK LATENCY DECISION (Task 4.4 Step 5): CSS-only, no vote_controller.js.
  Each stance button is a Turbo-driven button_to form; Turbo natively disables the
  submitter during the request and the same-origin round-trip is effectively instant,
  so a Stimulus controller would add nothing but code. Immediate press feedback comes
  from `active:scale-95` (CSS :active). Revisit only if a real deployment shows lag.

  DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.2) — docs/design-system/components/voting/VoteBars.prompt.md
  and VoteButton.prompt.md. Both halves of a row are spec'd to the pixel and neither is
  free to drift:

  - the button is CIRCULAR 44px (`w-11 h-11 rounded-full`) with a 2px stance border,
    white fill and a stance-coloured glyph — INVERTED to a solid stance fill with a
    white glyph when it is the viewer's vote. That inversion is the only "you voted"
    signal in the product, so `voted` drives colour, not an extra checkmark or badge.
  - the track is 8px (`h-2`) on `bg-gray-200` (`#e5e7eb`), filled by percentage in the
    stance colour, with the label right-aligned in a fixed 10-unit column so the three
    rows line up at any width.
  - press feedback is `active:scale-95` and nothing else: no ripple, no spinner, no
    fade. `transition` is here for that one transform.

  It does NOT go through `ds_button_classes`. That helper's every variant is a PILL
  with horizontal padding and a font size (`px-5 py-2 text-base` / `px-4 py-1 text-sm`);
  this is a fixed 44px square box with no text in it at all. Asking for it would mean
  overriding padding, width, height and font size — same-family Tailwind utilities,
  which resolve by their order in the bundle rather than by the order the caller wrote
  them (see the `padded:` note in ui/_card), so the overrides would be a coin flip
  rather than a decision. The `voted` fill would fight `bg-white` the same way.
  A circular icon button is a DIFFERENT component from the DS Button — VoteButton.jsx,
  not Button.jsx — and is spelled out here rather than bent out of the pill.

  Stance names are interpolated into `border-`/`bg-`/`fill-`/`text-`, which the Tailwind
  scanner cannot see; all four prefixes over the stance trio are covered by the
  `@source inline(...)` safelist in app/assets/tailwind/application.css (and `bg-white`
  /`text-white`/`fill-white` by the line under it). Adding a NEW interpolated prefix
  here means adding it there too.
%>
<%
  agree = hujah.agree_count.to_i
  neutral = hujah.neutral_count.to_i
  disagree = hujah.disagree_count.to_i
  total = agree + neutral + disagree
  rows = [["agree", 1, agree], ["neutral", 2, neutral], ["disagree", 3, disagree]]
%>
<div id="<%= dom_id(hujah, :vote_bars) %>" class="px-4 py-3">
  <% rows.each do |stance, choice, count| %>
    <% pct = total.zero? ? 0 : (count * 100.0 / total).round %>
    <% voted = current_user_vote == stance %>
    <% fill = voted ? "bg-#{stance} fill-white text-white" : "bg-white fill-#{stance} text-#{stance}" %>
    <div class="flex items-center mb-3 last:mb-0">
      <%= button_to hujah_votes_path(hujah.slug),
            params: { vote: choice },
            aria: { label: stance.capitalize, pressed: voted.to_s },
            class: "shrink-0 w-11 h-11 rounded-full border-2 border-#{stance} #{fill} " \
                   "flex items-center justify-center shadow transition active:scale-95" do %>
        <%= stance_icon(stance, class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <% end %>
      <div class="flex-1 mx-3 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded overflow-hidden">
        <div class="h-2 rounded bg-<%= stance %>" style="width: <%= pct %>%"></div>
      </div>
      <small class="w-10 text-right text-<%= stance %>"><%= pct %>%</small>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
